-- title:
--   Valuation ring of F inducing V on T and A on K
-- statement:
--   Let $K_1$, $K$, $T$, $F$ be fields, with $K$, $T$, $F$ all algebras over $K_1$, $F$ an algebra over both $K$ and $T$, and the two towers $K_1 \to K \to F$ and $K_1 \to T \to F$ compatible (both `IsScalarTower` hypotheses). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $K$ and $V$ a valuation subring of $T$. Assume two things. First, $A$ and $V$ agree on $K_1$: for every $x \in K_1$, the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $T$ lies in $V$. Second, $A$ is the only valuation subring of $K$ with its trace on $K_1$: every valuation subring $A'$ of $K$ such that, for all $x \in K_1$, the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $A'$ exactly when it lies in $A$, is equal to $A$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a valuation subring $\mathcal O$ of $F$ which simultaneously induces both: for every $t \in T$, the image of $t$ in $F$ lies in $\mathcal O$ if and only if $t \in V$, and for every $k \in K$, the image of $k$ in $F$ lies in $\mathcal O$ if and only if $k \in A$. No hypothesis is made that $F$ is generated by the images of $K$ and $T$, nor any normality or linear disjointness assumption.
--
--   This is the Chevalley extension theorem for places, in the form of a simultaneous prolongation: a valuation ring of $T$ is extended to the larger field $F$ in such a way that its trace on $K$ is the prescribed ring $A$, the uniqueness hypothesis on $A$ replacing any compatibility condition between the two subfields. It is used in the Igusa-tower arguments for modular curves at full level, where it supplies a valuation ring of a large field contracting to given valuation rings of the level field and of the coefficient field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_forall_mem_iff_of_forall_eq_of_agree.lean

